      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO PREPOSITIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A preposition connects nouns or pronouns to other words in a sentence to express relationships of time, place, direction, or purpose.",
        "The noun or pronoun following a preposition is its object and must always be in the objective case.",
        "'Since' is used to denote a specific point in time, while 'For' denotes a duration or period of time.",
        "'Beside' signifies 'by the side of', whereas 'Besides' means 'in addition to'.",
        "'In' and 'On' denote position/state, while 'Into' and 'Onto' denote motion and change of state."
      ],
      "id": "ac3c9ft"
    },
